# 04_SHAP_Analysis

`SHAP_XGBoost.R` reconstructs the XGBoost models fitted in the transfer benchmark and calculates TreeSHAP attributions on their held-out observations. It compares feature importance across schemes and stages, examines predictor dependence, and calculates pairwise TreeSHAP interactions on a balanced sample. Attributions describe the fitted model; they are not causal effects.

## Inputs

The script reads `benchmark_configuration.rds`, `outer_fold_manifest.csv`, `outer_split_specs.csv`, `oof_predictions.csv` and `fold_model_specifications.rds` from the folder 03 transfer run. Its default benchmark run ID is `multischeme_xgboost_paper_cum_2`, matching the supplied SHAP script. Set `PHENOLOGY_GENERALISATION_RUN_ID` or `PHENOLOGY_GENERALISATION_BENCHMARK_DIR` if your saved transfer results use a different directory. The script reads the predictor list and feature-set ID from that run's configuration, and requires the saved learner to be XGBoost.

The script uses the input path recorded in the benchmark configuration when it exists. If that old path is unavailable, it tries `Data/pheno_df_CV.csv` under the repository root. `PHENOLOGY_INPUT_FILE` overrides this choice. In every case, its MD5 checksum must match the input recorded for the transfer run. The installed `mlr3`, `mlr3learners` and `xgboost` versions must also match those recorded by the benchmark, and reconstructed out-of-fold predictions must pass the script's numerical agreement check.

## Run

From the repository root, the default run covers spatial-block and expanding-origin folds:

```bash
Rscript Scripts/04_SHAP_Analysis/SHAP_XGBoost.R
```

To analyse all five schemes used in the manuscript, run:

```bash
PHENOLOGY_SHAP_SCHEMES=spatial_block,leave_one_year_out,expanding_origin,environmental_zone,joint_space_time \
  Rscript Scripts/04_SHAP_Analysis/SHAP_XGBoost.R
```

Set `PHENOLOGY_PROJECT_DIR` when running outside the repository root. The default output directory is `shap_results/xgboost_generalisation_oof_treeshap_paper_cum_2/`; `PHENOLOGY_SHAP_RUN_ID` changes it. Run IDs should correspond to the transfer benchmark actually used. `PHENOLOGY_SHAP_RUN_INTERACTIONS=false` omits the computationally expensive interaction analysis. See the script's configuration section for sample sizes, worker counts, checkpoint settings and numerical tolerances.

## Outputs and interpretation

Key outputs include `global_shap_importance_macro_environment_stage.csv`, `shap_importance_by_exact_bbch.csv`, `shap_fold_stability.csv`, `oof_shap_values_wide.rds`, `shap_interaction_importance_all_pairs.csv`, `oof_shap_interactions_sample.rds`, figures under `plots/`, the analysis configuration and `session_info.txt`. Interactions are calculated for a capped, environment–stage-balanced sample rather than every held-out row. The output directories also contain fold diagnostics and input-support audits.